  message: "Fixed in PR #1192 (9e8ed17fca, plus 9f2e8f06d7 for coverage). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tipoh_09242026/.\n\nROOT CAUSE (verified in code): the import hint scala and kotlin pass the resolver is a DOTTED path, and the resolver compares it against FILE paths, so it never matched. An exact name match also returns before any hint is read.\n\nTHE ASKS:\n1. An explicit import outranks a same-named project symbol in another package, unless the import names a project path. Done in the producers.\n   - kotlin: exact qualified-name check; the Companion segment is dropped. When the returned symbol is not the imported one, the call binds the project symbol AT the imported path (from a map of every file's symbols), or else is withheld.\n   - scala: a lenient check (relative imports, nested types, package objects, a relative-to-object reading, renamed-package imports, _root_). Block-scoped imports apply only inside their block. A contradicted call is left unresolved with the import path in its module slot.\n   - A project type keeps the placeholder module slot when its import names a project path (WI-kilap).\n2. MEASURED as a set, call sites diffed (src, line, callee), dev 99281e3c43 vs the fix. Scala, 11 repos: 5,631 resolved -> unresolved, plus 666 slot-only changes. A random sample of 30 on the final code: all 30 had been false edges.\n3. Detekt's imported project type (the WI-kilap regression test) still resolves. That test passed in CI.\n4. kotlin HAS the same shape (checked: `import java.io.File` then `File(\"x\")` bound a project `class File`) and is fixed here. On 5 repos, 5,426 calls were re-targeted to the imported symbol and 2,404 withheld (2,346 of those are AssertJ assertThat on detekt).\n\nTHE FILED INSTANCES, re-run:\n- spark: dev binds 14 calls to the test `case class Process`, 13 of them false. 10 now carry scala.sys.process.Process and classify as a launch (test_jvm_import_outranks_project_name.py pins it through classify_call). The other 3 import through a WILDCARD, which this row's statement does not cover. Filed as WI-kifim.\n- scala3: does NOT reproduce on the current checkout. dev binds TestScripts' `Process(script)` to the stdlib source scala3 vendors (library/src/scala/sys/process/Process.scala). That is the imported symbol, and the fix keeps it.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED:\n- WI-niriz: scala cannot re-target without qualified names; a member inherited through an object is wrongly withheld (1 in a sample of 25).\n- WI-kifim: wildcard imports.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that every scala withhold is right. The first sample of 25 found 3 wrong. Two of those shapes are fixed here; the third is in WI-niriz."  # 0971
